"""Scalar-only projection of the immutable pgwire limit contract.

`PgWireLinuxLimits` is a configuration aggregate owned by the server creator.
It must not be returned by a native worker/registry operation.  This module
copies the one control value needed for admission into a small immutable
snapshot.  Consumers crossing an execution boundary read only the `i64`
result from `max_sessions`; no aggregate, class, enum, text, `Any`, or raw
pointer is transported.

Ownership contract:

* The caller owns the source `PgWireLinuxLimits` and may discard or replace it
  after `pgwire_max_sessions_snapshot` returns.
* `PgWireMaxSessionsSnapshot` owns its copied scalar value for its whole
  lifetime.  It has no reference into the source aggregate and is safe to
  freeze/share as a value.
* `pgwire_max_sessions` is a read-only scalar projection.  It does not retain
  the receiver, mutate state, or create a loan.  A worker may copy the result;
  the parent remains the owner of admission state and performs all commits.
* A non-positive source bound is normalized to `1`, matching
  `PgWireLinuxLimits.create`'s fail-closed capacity policy.  No unbounded
  value can enter a worker descriptor through this operation.
"""

use nogc_sync_mut.database.postgres_mimic.linux_limits.{PgWireLinuxLimits}

struct PgWireMaxSessionsSnapshot:
    value: i64

fn pgwire_max_sessions_snapshot(limits: PgWireLinuxLimits) -> PgWireMaxSessionsSnapshot:
    val bounded = if limits.max_sessions > 0: limits.max_sessions else: 1
    PgWireMaxSessionsSnapshot(value: bounded)

fn pgwire_max_sessions(snapshot: PgWireMaxSessionsSnapshot) -> i64:
    snapshot.value

export PgWireMaxSessionsSnapshot
export pgwire_max_sessions_snapshot, pgwire_max_sessions
